note('Author page 1, archive number 43: a new sequence begins, with an explicit warning about the preceding notation. It sets up a conformal sphere with a three-point subset, the direct symmetry group and the involution τ, then introduces a homogeneous invariant metric and the two-element orientation/component sets. The marginal Stokes convention relates these three sets by the three written cyclic isomorphisms. The ink, enlarged, settles ≠1 rather than +1. The exponent of the positive scalar remains uncertain (*+ versus ++); no mathematical normalisation is imposed. The dark V in E\\V is written over horizontal remnants. R_J is retained as written in the last paragraph, beside the earlier family (R_i). No external claim or uniqueness proof was checked; this note reports the page. The note says the antipodal map does not stabilise J. The two small cancellations in the τ sentence remain weak.')
hand('near-vertical inequality slash and capital J','The ≠ sign can resemble a plus when the second bar is faint; scan 044 supplies two bars in the enlarged τ sentence. The capital subscript J is angular and undotted; C doubted J/i and H used j at the generators of V. These observations are local, not a claim about every occurrence.')
